    "body": "A shared random shift pool can cover every ordered point pair under an explicit joint-character density condition. The global event supports adaptive reuse without selected-output uniformity. Nine generic finite-support/pool laws and actual prime-field subgroup/gate probes are checked locally; the character-sum and real exponential applications remain hand analysis. [pcc:unverified]\n\n- Canonical all-tracked-source gate: exit0, 258 audited theorems, 0 failing, 0 trusted-native exceptions; nine named compiler axiom prints use only allowed standard axioms. All four PDF pages inspected. [pcc:unverified]\n- Six-field proof map: docs/universal-shift-pool-20261116-plan.md. Report, editable diagram, primary-source hashes and publication scope: docs/universal-shift-pool-20261116/. [pcc:unverified]\n- PCC-20261116-8ad24e is interpretive/unverified. Old nine-row ledger prefix and all91 subject hashes retained. Prior PR24 closing autonomy/lessons are included; owner autonomy8/0 and lessons17/0 checks pass. [pcc:unverified]\n\nThe pool supplies retention and capped scans of known pairs. Capped implicit original-tuple extraction and useful nonzero-relation yield remain open. No executable, measured speed, numerical/native, paid or qualification run is claimed. Hosted checks must be inspected at the actual published head; local compiler evidence does not establish hosted CI success.\n\nPublished head0afe2ec517020bdc7768e1c74b89615766f39454 remains open. Same-head CI43820138347 failed: build-and-audit133141103092 and selftest133141103372 both have zero steps and explicit account billing-lock annotations. No hosted pass or retry. GitHub rejected the default head-guarded auto-merge attempt because repository allow_auto_merge is false; repository settings are unchanged. [pcc:unverified]\n",
